        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "914962d7-c386-5f9a-a0a5-dca7434b3fdd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elia Kazan, William Inge, David Amram, Zohra Lampert, Natalie Wood, Warren Beatty\n- Products: Splendor in the Grass, Let's Scare Jessica to Death, Alphabet City\n- Topics: film direction, screenwriting, acting, film music\n\nFacts:\n- Elia Kazan was born as Elias Kazantzoglou on September 7, 1909, and he died on September 28, 2003.\n- Elia Kazan was a Greek-American director, producer, writer, and actor whom The New York Times described as one of the most honored and influential directors in Broadway and Hollywood history.\n- Splendor in the Grass is a 1961 Technicolor drama film about a teenage girl dealing with sexual repression, love, and heartbreak.\n- William Inge wrote Splendor in the Grass, briefly appeared in it as a Protestant clergyman, and won an Oscar for its screenplay.\n- Elia Kazan directed Splendor in the Grass, and David Amram composed its score.\n- Zohra Lampert starred alongside Natalie Wood and Warren Beatty in Splendor in the Grass.\n- Zohra Lampert was born on May 13, 1937.\n- Zohra Lampert is an American actress with film, television, and stage roles, including the title role in the 1971 cult horror film Let's Scare Jessica to Death.\n- In Alphabet City, Zohra Lampert played Johnny's mother.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4238d82f-261b-50a5-83bb-dd5eb381779b",
        "text": "Page: Splendor in the Grass. Sentence: Splendor in the Grass is a 1961 Technicolor drama film that tells a story of a teenage girl navigating her feelings of sexual repression, love, and heartbreak.\nPage: Splendor in the Grass. Sentence: Written by William Inge, who appears briefly as a Protestant clergyman and who won an Oscar for his screenplay, the film was directed by Elia Kazan and features a score by jazz composer David Amram.\nPage: Elia Kazan. Sentence: Elia Kazan (born Elias Kazantzoglou September 7, 1909 – September 28, 2003) was a Greek-American director, producer, writer and actor, described by \"The New York Times\" as \"one of the most honored and influential directors in Broadway and Hollywood history\".\nPage: Zohra Lampert. Sentence: Zohra Lampert (born May 13, 1937) is an American actress, who has had roles on film, television and stage including as the title character in the 1971 cult horror film \"Let's Scare Jessica to Death\", as well as for starring alongside Natalie Wood and Warren Beatty in the 1961 \"Splendor in the Grass\".\nPage: Alphabet City (film). Sentence: Acclaimed film and stage actress Zohra Lampert plays Johnny's mother.",
